{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And He brought them out</b> — They are the ones going out, for the listener may be uncertain; therefore he did not bother to explain \"Israel.\" And behold, he returns to the word \"Israel\": a stranger in the land of Ham, and He brought them out." "<b>and none among His tribes stumbled</b> — needy, as in: והמכשלה הזאת. And it is possible that it is as its plain meaning." "<b>The sense of \"among His tribes\"</b> — although they are many."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 105, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:33.481401385Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}